---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_460",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 460,
  "text": "[[2043.1]] <b>373.  Animadversio in philosophiam Cartesii [Frühjahr 1689 bis Herbst 1689 (?)]</b>\n [[2043.2]] <tab/>[Frühjahr 1689 bis Herbst 1689 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[2043.7]] Cartesii doctrinam et ingenium semper mirifice veneratus sum, saepeque immaturae\n[[2043.8]] ejus morti indolui, nec dubito, quin multa et magna daturus fuisset in usum generis\n[[2043.9]] humani si ad Hobbii aut Robervallii aetatem pervenisset. Et vellem sectatores Magistri\n[[2043.10]] praeclara cogitata prosequi potius, quam repetere tantum ut plerumque solent, et sub alio\n[[2043.11]] verborum schemate repraesentare. Sed nescio quo fato fit, ut philosophiae isti, quae\n[[2043.12]] profundas Geometriae meditationes et multiplicia naturae experimenta exigit, plures ex\n[[2043.13]] illis se applicent qui sub titulo magnitudinum figurarum et motuum, speciosam potius et\n[[2043.14]] auribus secundam disserendi de oblatis facilitatem, atque sui ostentationem, quam solidam\n[[2043.15]] rerum notitiam quaerunt, magno damno juventutis, quae scholasticas quisquilias\n[[2043.16]] permutans hodie aliis quisquiliis animum majorum capacem iis implet, quae usum postea\n[[2043.17]] in vita et disciplinis non habent. Neque enim aut Chymicus experimenta futura ex\n[[2043.18]] ramorum, hamorum atque aculeorum consideratione qualem hactenus habemus providebit,\n[[2043.19]] aut mechanicus, neque medicus scire poterit, quibus dosibus materiae subtilis aut\n[[2043.20]] particularum striatarum febris curetur; neque hydraulicis anguillares aquae partes ullum\n[[2043.21]] adjumentum afferent. Itaque etsi haec vera essent, longe tamen ab iis adhuc absunt,\n[[2043.22]] quibus est opus, et ignavia est tam levibus et remotis contentum esse velle. </p>\n<p> [[2043.23]] Equidem Cartesius alicubi in <i>Epistolis</i> spem facit constituendae verae Medicinae, si\n[[2043.24]] adhuc aliquae sibi observationes darentur, et sane defuere subtilissimo viro necessaria ad\n[[2044.1]] constituendam philosophiam experimenta, sed quotusquisque ex sectatoribus ejus in tanta\n[[2044.2]] novorum experimentorum luce ad exequenda Magistri destinata animum attollit. Quam\n[[2044.3]] jejuna sunt quae de salibus notavit Cartesius quibus tamen omnis chymia fere\n[[2044.4]] superstruenda est, quam levia et rudia, quae de mineralibus et metallis. De homine\n[[2044.5]] quoque sciunt jam plerique magis ex ingenio quam natura philosophatum esse. </p>\n<p> [[2044.6]] Sed mihi ut quod res est dicam insigni huic viro nihil magis nocuisse videtur quam\n[[2044.7]] ambitio constituendae novae sectae. Hinc omnis et fons malorum. Ideo enim et praematura\n[[2044.8]] multa nec satis absoluta protrusit in publicum, et de plerisque aliis viris egregiis\n[[2044.9]] indigne et cum contemtu locutus est, quemadmodum ex <i>Epistolis</i> apparet. Et aliorum\n[[2044.10]] praeclara inventa sibi arte vindicavit, exiguo aut nullo grati animi judicio. Unde non\n[[2044.11]] potuit non invidiae se exponere, et odia incitare, et in contentiones incidere, quibus ipsi\n[[2044.12]] bona temporis pars melioribus destinata periit. Quis non cum admiratione et propemodum\n[[2044.13]] cum indignatione legat quam contemtim de Galilaeo et de Fermatio aliisque\n[[2044.14]] excellentibus viris loquatur in <i>Epistolis</i>. Objectiones ejus in Methodum de maximis et\n[[2044.15]] minimis Fermatianam sophismata erant contorta, et quae in Galilaei motuum scientiam\n[[2044.16]] notat tanquam gravia descendentia longe ab his legibus dissentirent, ea testimonio naturae,\n[[2044.17]] et successu experimentorum refutantur. Quis autem credat quod in <i>Epistolis</i> asserit\n[[2044.18]] Vietam sibi non lectum cum satis compertum videatur, non Vietae tantum sed et Harrioti\n[[2044.19]] qui Vietam prosecutus est inventis usum esse. Certe magna libri <i>Geometriae</i> tertii pars\n[[2044.20]] Harrioto innititur, qui jam et aequationes nihilo aequales posuerat, et ex radicibus in se\n[[2044.21]] invicem ductis oriri notaverat. Recessum corporum a circulo per tangentem et rationem\n[[2044.22]] hinc explicandi detrusionem gravium ad centrum debebat Keplero, idem primus Hyperbolam\n[[2044.23]] satisfacere refractionibus subodoratus erat. Veram legem dioptricae ex Snellii\n[[2045.1]] ineditis Cartesium hausisse patefecit Isaacus Vossius, demonstrationem Snellii vel non\n[[2045.2]] viderat, vel studio mutavit, ut rem sibi propriam redderet, sed coactus est in pejus ire, et\n[[2045.3]] aëri plus resistentiae quam aquae aut vitro tribuere, ut diceret aliquid Snellio non dictum\n[[2045.4]] et ne sic quidem examini accurato satisfecit, et sane nec potuit, dum gloriae maluit quam\n[[2045.5]] veritati servire. </p>\n<p> [[2045.6]] Nec dubium est, quin Maurolyci et M. Antonii de Dominis cogitata <i>de iride</i> meditantem\n[[2045.7]] juverint, quorum neminem mentione dignatus est, quemadmodum nec Gilbertum\n[[2045.8]] cujus magnetica inventa maximam ipsi lucem attulerant. </p>\n",
  "number": "373.",
  "title": "Animadversio in philosophiam Cartesii",
  "date": "[Frühjahr 1689 bis Herbst 1689 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:373. Animadversio in philosophiam Cartesii [Frühjahr 1689 bis Herbst 1689 (?)] [Frühjahr 1689 bis Herbst 1689 (?)] Cartesii doctrinam et ingenium semper mirifice veneratus sum, saepeque immaturae ejus morti indolui, nec dubito, quin multa et magna daturus fuisset in usum generis humani si ad Hobbii ...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>